.TH CWE-122 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-122 \- Heap\-based Buffer Overflow
.SH RANK
2025 CWE Top 25 rank: \fB#16\fR (2024 rank: NEW).
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: Memory Safety.
.SH DESCRIPTION
An overflow of a heap\-allocated buffer. Overrunning it corrupts adjacent heap objects or allocator metadata; with heap grooming this becomes a reliable code execution primitive. Common in parsers. A C/C++ class.
.SH MITIGATION
Allocate based on the actual required size and bound every copy by it. Validate length fields and use checked arithmetic for size calculations to avoid integer overflow. In C++ prefer std::vector. Test with AddressSanitizer.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB33\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
